  "usage_note": "**Thought** is also the past tense and past participle of **think**. As a noun, it is countable for one idea (*a thought*) and uncountable for the act of thinking (*much thought*).",
  "learner_errors": [
    {
      "incorrect": "In my thought, the plan is too expensive.",
      "correct": "In my opinion, the plan is too expensive.",
      "note": "To give your opinion, use **in my opinion** or **I think**; *in my thought* is not used."
    },
    {
      "incorrect": "I gave many thoughts to the problem.",
      "correct": "I gave a lot of thought to the problem.",
      "note": "For thinking carefully, **thought** is uncountable: **a lot of thought**, **much thought**."
